{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FAy7LwTGzGr4X99ppPA2jg","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-3tmvoseq\ntotal 16\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff     128 Oct  2 17:14 .\ndrwx------@ 13547 brenn  staff  433504 Oct  2 17:14 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    13 brenn  staff     416 Oct  2 12:20 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff    4960 Oct  2 17:14 sheet.md\n# N/A challenge: R04 — Retrieval-corpus integrity\n\nThe reviewer says this item's feature or exposure is absent. **Try to disprove that\nclaim.** Trace the harness, tools, integrations, peer messages, and indirect paths;\nnames and README claims are not enough. Explain what you searched and found.\n\n**The requirement:** The retrieval corpus is the set of documents the agent searches for context. Its index stores those documents, or smaller passages called chunks, in a search engine or vector database. Limit which identities and sources can add or change content there. For each chunk, keep its source, when it was added, its trust level, and its access permissions. Enforce the requesting tenant's access when searching. Test an unapproved attempt to add content and a search across tenants. Also test quarantining, expiring, and revoking access to seeded test documents. Confirm the affected chunks disappear from search results and caches within a stated time. See the [R04 recipe](CHECKLIST-VERIFICATION.md#r--run-time).\n**N/A when:** Only when the agent has no retrieval corpus or search index.\n**Reviewer's claim:** The agent has no retrieval corpus or search index; documents are read by id only.\n**Reviewer's evidence:** [{\"file\": \"release/manifest.yaml\", \"line\": 91, \"note\": \"retrieval: none; documents are read by doc_id only (tools/documents.py:24)\"}]\n\nSet `applicability` to **absent** only when the N/A condition holds, **present**\nwhen you find the feature or exposure, or **unclear** when you cannot establish\nabsence. Include `evidence` (path:line), `quote` (exact code), and `note` (paths\nsearched and why the condition holds or fails) at the top level of your verdict.\nIf present, evaluate the checks below: a failed control makes this a gap; if you\ncannot show a failed control, it becomes needs_evidence. Never turn it into a pass.\nIf absent, use verdict upheld; if unclear, use verdict unclear.\n\n\n## R04.1\n\n**Check:** Only named identities and sources can add or change index content, and the ingestion path checks the writer.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find index write paths (`upsert`, `add_documents`, `index`, ingestion jobs). 2) Check each verifies the writer identity or source against a named list. 3) Answer no if any write path, including the agent's own tools or an admin endpoint, accepts writes without that check.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no search index or retrieval corpus (manifest retrieval: none); documents are read by id only.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## R04.2\n\n**Check:** Each stored chunk has metadata for source, time added, trust level, and access permissions.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find chunk write code and metadata fields. 2) Check source, time added, trust level, and access permissions are stored on every chunk. 3) Answer no if any field is missing, or set only on some ingestion paths.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no retrieval corpus.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## R04.3\n\n**Check:** Search applies the requesting tenant's access filter at query time, in the store or retrieval code, not after the model answers.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find search calls (`similarity_search`, `query`, `search`, `filter=`, `where=`). 2) Check a tenant or access filter is applied in the store query, from the caller's identity. 3) Answer no if filtering happens after retrieval or in the prompt, the filter is optional, or the tenant comes from a model-supplied argument.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no search call exists; read_document filters by business_unit and doc_id.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## R04.4\n\n**Check:** Code can quarantine, expire, and revoke chunks, and it also clears or invalidates search caches.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find quarantine, expiry, and revoke code (`delete`, `quarantine`, `ttl`, `expires_at`). 2) Check search excludes those chunks and caches are cleared. 3) Answer no if any of the three operations is missing, or caches (query cache, embedding cache) are not invalidated.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no index or search cache to invalidate.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to R04.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"R04\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R04.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\nagent\nagent/migrations\nagent/migrations/001_init.sql\nagent/app\nagent/app/killswitch.py\nagent/app/ingest.py\nagent/app/startup.py\nagent/app/tools\nagent/app/tools/payments.py\nagent/app/tools/erp.py\nagent/app/tools/memory.py\nagent/app/tools/documents.py\nagent/app/tools/__init__.py\nagent/app/tools/slack.py\nagent/app/audit.py\nagent/app/approvals.py\nagent/app/budget.py\nagent/app/__init__.py\nagent/app/extractor.py\nagent/app/redact.py\nagent/app/ga